=== RH12 PRIME-GAS SELF-DUALITY CHECK ===
K1 REGISTERED BEFORE COMPUTING: no normalized prime-gas log-moment
  curve crosses 1/2 at or below sigma = 1 (M diverges there; R = M/ln zeta
  undefined for sigma <= 1); predicted R(sigma) in (0.80, 1) for sigma > 1
  -> the prime-gas moment does NOT single out the critical line.
MUTATE = 0 (exponent distortion 1.0)

sieve: 78498 primes < 1000000

--- (1) EXACT STATEMENT xi(s) = xi(1-s) (numeric check, 40 dps) ---
  xi(0.5) - xi(0.5)  |res| = 0.0
  xi((1+2j)) - xi(-2j)  |res| = 1.1485e-41
  xi((0.5 + 5.0j)) - xi((0.5 - 5.0j))  |res| = 3.00211e-42
  xi((0.5 + 14.134725j)) - xi((0.5 - 14.134725j))  |res| = 4.50635e-50
  xi((0.5 + 21.0j)) - xi((0.5 - 21.0j))  |res| = 1.76772e-48
  xi((2.5+0j)) - xi((-1.5+0j))  |res| = 0.0
  xi((3.7+0j)) - xi((-2.7+0j))  |res| = 2.29589e-41
  xi((-1.5+0j)) - xi((2.5+0j))  |res| = 0.0
  xi((-10.5+0j)) - xi((11.5+0j))  |res| = 0.0
  xi((0.25+30j)) - xi((0.75-30j))  |res| = 3.82495e-49
  max |xi(s)-xi(1-s)| over 10 points = 2.29589e-41
  exact statement: xi(s) = xi(1-s) for ALL s in C (Riemann FE, a theorem);
  s = 1/2 is the fixed point of the involution s -> 1-s; AT s = 1/2 the
  identity is tautological (both sides are xi(1/2)).
  xi(1/2) = 0.49712077818831410991   (zeta(1/2) = -1.46035450881)
  ln zeta(2) = 0.49770030247074534747;  |xi(1/2) - ln zeta(2)| = 0.000579524
    -> agree through 3 significant digits (0.497), differ in the 4th;
    registered COINCIDENCE (no mechanism, no claim).
  prime-gas facts at s = 1/2: sum_p p^{-1/2} diverges (PNT) -> the Euler
  product prod (1-p^{-1/2})^{-1} DIVERGES: the prime-gas partition function
  does not exist at the self-dual temperature T = 1/s = 2; zeta(1/2) is
  analytic continuation of the product, which converges only for Re s > 1.

