  EXACT all-prime handling (the (sigma-1)-handling):
    identity: prod_p (1+p^-sigma) = prod_p (1-p^-2sigma)/(1-p^-sigma)
             = zeta(sigma)/zeta(2sigma)   (sigma > 1)   [exact]
    -> M_full(sigma) = ln zeta(sigma) - ln zeta(2sigma)  (exact, all primes)
    -> as sigma -> 1+:  M_full(sigma) = -ln(sigma-1) - ln zeta(2) + o(1)
       residue EXACT: C = -ln zeta(2) = -0.49770030247074534747
    sigma=1.001: M_full=    6.411770   M_cut(10^6)=    2.693293   (missing tail +3.718477)
    sigma=1.010: M_full=    4.124458   M_cut(10^6)=    2.588802   (missing tail +1.535656)
    sigma=1.050: M_full=    2.579536   M_cut(10^6)=    2.199166   (missing tail +0.380370)
    sigma=1.100: M_full=    1.960245   M_cut(10^6)=    1.840731   (missing tail +0.119514)
    sigma=1.500: M_full=    0.776226   M_cut(10^6)=    0.776098   (missing tail +0.000128)
    sigma=2.000: M_full=    0.418590   M_cut(10^6)=    0.418590   (missing tail +0.000000)
    -> the cutoff sum is exact for sigma >= ~1.5 (tail < 2e-4) and misses
       the logarithmically divergent tail for sigma -> 1+; R below uses M_full.

  normalized R(sigma) = M(sigma)/ln zeta(sigma) -- EXACT curve R = 1 - ln zeta(2s)/ln zeta(s):
    sigma=1.001: R = 0.928121   (ln zeta(2s)/ln zeta(s) = 0.071879)
    sigma=1.010: R = 0.894495   (ln zeta(2s)/ln zeta(s) = 0.105505)
    sigma=1.050: R = 0.852919   (ln zeta(2s)/ln zeta(s) = 0.147081)
