    sigma=2.000: R = 0.841049   (ln zeta(2s)/ln zeta(s) = 0.158951)
    R -> 1 as sigma -> 1+ (ln zeta(2s) finite while ln zeta(s) diverges)
    R -> 1 as sigma -> inf (ratio ~ 2^-sigma); R stays in (0.805, 1), max deficit 0.195
    min R = 0.804706 at sigma = 1.351;  max ln zeta(2s)/ln zeta(s) = 0.195294 at sigma = 1.351  (< 1/2 = 0.5 by 0.305)
    sigma_c with R = 1/2 in (1,2]: NONE  -> K1 CONFIRMED: no crossing at 1/2,
    the prime-gas moment does not single out the critical line.
  raw crossing with kappa=1/2: M(sigma_star) = 1/2 at sigma_star = 1.838323
    (exists on the RAW curve -- but sigma_star ~ 1.84 is NOT 1/2, NOT 3/2,
     NOT 2: at no framework axis; the framework axis 3/2 gives
     M(3/2) = 0.776098 vs pi/4 = 0.785398 -- near-miss 1.18% off, COINCIDENCE at the framework axis)
    M(2) = 0.418590 < 1/2;  dM/dsigma(3/2) = -1.173590 (derivative at framework axis, data)
  secondary normalization M(sigma)/sum_p p^-sigma (cutoff): min 0.9138 (never 1/2)

--- (3) CRITICAL-LINE LOG-MOMENT OF THE PRIMES (sigma = 1/2) ---
  S_half = sum over p<10^6 of ln(1 + p^-1/2) = 175.1141240275
    cutoff x=1000     : S(1/2;x) =    11.758253   (PNT leading 2*sqrt(x)/ln x =     9.1557)
    cutoff x=10000    : S(1/2;x) =    28.107688   (PNT leading 2*sqrt(x)/ln x =    21.7147)
    cutoff x=100000   : S(1/2;x) =    68.903842   (PNT leading 2*sqrt(x)/ln x =    54.9344)
    cutoff x=1000000  : S(1/2;x) =   175.114124   (PNT leading 2*sqrt(x)/ln x =   144.7648)
    -> S_half grows without bound (like ~2*sqrt(x)/ln(x), PNT; the data above
       are monotone unbounded): the TOTAL over all primes is +infinity, so the
       share of ANY finite prime set -> 0.
  ratio to the (finite) framework-axis moment: S_half / M(3/2) = 225.6342
  ratio to the (divergent) total: S_half / infinity = 0 (share of the p<10^6 block)
  share of first Euler factor p=2 at sigma=1/2: 0.3054% of S_half
  share of p in {2,3,5}  at sigma=1/2: 0.7767% of S_half
    at sigma=1.0: p=2 share = 14.99%, p in {2,3,5} share = 32.36% of M(1.0)
    at sigma=1.5: p=2 share = 39.01%, p in {2,3,5} share = 72.72% of M(1.5)
    at sigma=2.0: p=2 share = 53.31%, p in {2,3,5} share = 87.85% of M(2.0)

--- (4) VERDICT ---
K1 CONFIRMED (registered pre-computation, matches data): R(sigma) never equals 1/2,
R_min = 0.805 > 1/2; the prime-gas log-moment M(sigma) singles out NO point at or
below the critical line -- it DIVERGES there (no partition function at T = 2).
The zeta's own self-duality xi(s) = xi(1-s) holds exactly at ALL s (theorem); the
framework's M(s) = M(3-s) (axis 3/2, Lean-certified) is a DIFFERENT object (zero-free
beta, per RH07) and neither axis is a prime-gas temperature.  NO claim of RH.

